skate3-gmod

native/skate-bridge/src/rails.rs and parts of native/skate-bridge/src/collision.rs
are ported from 2010 Rust Rewrite Mashup by chasmlol
(https://github.com/chasmlol/2010-rust-rewrite-mashup, commit f608f85),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Changes: the math types come
from glam instead of Bevy, and MW2-specific extraction was removed.

setup/convert.py is adapted from that project's skate/converter/iw4l_skate_convert.py
under the same license.

The playermodel retarget in addon/lua/skate3/cl_skater.lua is ported from that
project's crates/render_anim/src/skate/rig.rs, and the board import in
native/gmod-skate/src/skater.rs follows its crates/assets/src/skate_board.rs,
under the same license.

native/patches/skate-host-hud.patch modifies that project's skate-host crate
(at the same commit) to report the trick line in progress and set the skater's stance, under the same
license. CI applies it to a fresh clone; none of that crate is copied here.

The setup app bundles vgmstream-cli (https://github.com/vgmstream/vgmstream),
which decodes the sounds on the player's own disc. Its licence ships beside it
as COPYING; the Windows build's FFmpeg and codec libraries are vgmstream's own
distribution, unchanged.

Which Skate 3 sound ids play the pops, landings and grind hits, and the
layout of the game's SPLC sound banks, come from the reverse-engineering notes
in doriangironde/skate-3-rust-macos (https://github.com/doriangironde/skate-3-rust-macos)
and Hailey-Ross's audio work on SK8-ENGINE/skate-3-rust-engine (PR #32). No
code is taken from either; setup/audio.py is written from those notes.

setup/skate3_formats/ reads the park pieces and the Mega Park stadium off the
player's own disc. archive.py, arena.py, geometry.py, world_materials.py and
world_textures.py come from NativeX World Studio
(https://github.com/NativeXex/nativex-world-studio-skate3), MIT licensed
(LICENSE-NativeX.txt); archive.py is changed to read stored chunks.
skate3_streams.py and retail_collision_mesh.py come from SK8-Engine
(https://github.com/SK8-ENGINE/SK8-Engine, tree 311cd40), MIT licensed
(LICENSE-SK8-ENGINE.txt), as NativeX vendors them. See that folder's README.
